## Credits

Several skills in this stack grew from **Superpowers** by Jesse Vincent
(https://github.com/obra/superpowers, also distributed as the official
`superpowers` Claude Code plugin) — MIT licensed. In particular
`using-git-worktrees`, `tdd`, `receiving-code-review`, `commit-work`,
`finish-branch`, `resolving-merge-conflicts`, and `handoff` descend from its
skills, and the execution engine's shape — a fresh implementer per task, a
review after each, a broad review at the end — follows its
`subagent-driven-development`.

Other material this stack leans on:

- **John Ousterhout**, *A Philosophy of Software Design* — the deep-module
  vocabulary and "Design It Twice" in `codebase-design`.
- **Martin Fowler**, *Refactoring* (ch. 3) — the code-smell baseline the
  Standards axis and the task reviewer carry.
